  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-3,1),(1,-4),(1,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{\u2032},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{90}^{\u2218}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{\u2218}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(-1,3)$\n- $(4,1)$\n- $(0,-1)$",
  "worked_solution": "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{90}^{\u2218}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{\u2218}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{90}^{\u2218}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,-3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,\\,-4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{90}^{\u2218}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\,-3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,\\,-4 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{\u2032}$ are $(-1,-3),(4,1),(0,1).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
